sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-004: Email-Based Login Two-Factor Authentication — MFA Login Sequence
    actor User
    participant UI as React Login + OTP UI
    participant Firebase as Firebase Authentication
    participant API as Express Auth API
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL
    participant Mail as Email Delivery

    User->>UI: Complete password or Google/GitHub primary sign-in
    UI->>Firebase: Authenticate primary credential
    Firebase-->>UI: Verified pre-MFA identity and ID token
    alt Password primary authentication
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/mfa/challenge with Bearer token
    else OAuth primary authentication
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/oauth/sign-in with provider ID token
    end
    API->>Firebase: Verify token, email, provider, and revocation as applicable
    API->>DB: Load active participant and recent account attempts
    alt Suspended, unverified, locked, or unauthorized
        API-->>UI: Explicit 401/403/423, no challenge/session
    else Eligible for challenge
        API->>API: Enforce one send per 60 seconds and five per hour
        API->>API: Generate cryptographically random 6-digit OTP
        API->>DB: Invalidate pending challenges
        API->>DB: INSERT hash verifier with expires_at = now + 10 minutes
        API->>Mail: Send raw OTP to verified email
        alt Delivery fails
            Mail--xAPI: Delivery error
            API->>DB: Invalidate pending challenge
            API-->>UI: 502 retryable failure, no session
        else Delivery succeeds
            Mail-->>User: Email containing one-time code
            API-->>UI: Challenge ID, masked email, 600-second lifetime
            UI-->>User: Show six-digit input and countdown, no protected access
        end
    end

    opt User requests resend
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/mfa/challenge
        API->>DB: Preserve failures, invalidate predecessor, create new challenge
        API-->>UI: New challenge or 429 rate-limit guidance
    end

    User->>UI: Submit six-digit code
    UI->>API: POST /api/auth/mfa/verify<br/>{challengeId, code}
    API->>DB: Load participant-bound challenge and account attempts
    alt Missing, invalidated, consumed, or time >= expires_at
        API-->>UI: Explicit invalid/expired/consumed response
    else Challenge is current
        API->>DB: Atomic compare-and-set consume using challenge ID and OTP hash
        alt Code is incorrect
            DB-->>API: No row consumed
            API->>DB: INSERT failed mfa_attempt
            alt This is the fifth consecutive failure
                API->>DB: Invalidate outstanding challenges
                API-->>UI: 423 locked for 15 minutes
            else Fewer than five failures
                API-->>UI: Incorrect-code response, remain pre-MFA
            end
        else Code matches and one consume wins
            API->>DB: INSERT successful mfa_attempt
            API->>Firebase: Set mfa_auth_time = current auth_time
            API-->>UI: 200 verified
            UI->>Firebase: Force-refresh ID token
            UI->>API: Protected request with current MFA claim
            API-->>UI: Authorized only if token, active account, MFA, and role pass
            UI-->>User: Render protected function
        end
    end

    Note over UI,DB: Current discrepancy: the React challenge/code path does not compare the token auth_time<br/>with the prior lock end after lock expiry, although the alternate send/otp path does.

